# Worker pool

How the tool schedules tasks across parallel workers.

## Sizing the pool

The pool starts 4 workers by default. Set `workers` in [the configuration file](http://fixture.test/config) to change it.

Defaults by platform

| Platform | Workers | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Linux | 4 | Uses `epoll` |
| macOS | 4 | Uses kqueue \| fallback |
| Windows | 2 |  |

### Steps

1. Measure the task duration.
2. Pick a size:
   - CPU-bound: one worker per core
   - I/O-bound: two to four per core
3. Restart the service.

```yaml
# example.yaml
workers: 8
timeout: 30
```

> Too many workers can slow things down.
>
> Measure before and after.

Special characters stay literal: 2 \* 3 \< 7 \& \[x\] \| \_y\_ #1.

